    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/9jg1pw26y3": {
      "title": "Bioinformatician position in cancer research (F/M)",
      "description": "Bioinformatician position in cancer research (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Bioinformatician position in cancer research (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  04/01/2027 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center France’s leading cancer research and treatment centre, Institut Curie unites a renowned research centre and a specialist hospital, fostering close collaboration between scientists, clinicians and healthcare professionals. It offers an environment of excellence where expertise comes together around shared values: care, humanity, openness, collaboration, efficiency, innovation, solidarity and commitment. Missions Activités principales Laboratory \"Chemical Biology of Cancer\" Unit - Director: Fatima Mechta-Grigoriou Institut Curie -  U1339 Inserm - UMR3666 CNRS “Stress and Cancer” Laboratory - Director: Fatima Mechta-Grigoriou https://curie.fr/equipe/mechta-grigoriou This position is associated with the ARTURO project, funded by the European Commission under the Horizon Europe programme (Cancer Mission 2023). International collaboration between Institut Curie and Assistance Publique Hôpitaux de Paris - Bichat hospital (France), Universidade Catolica Portugueasa and Fundação Gaspar Frutuoso (Portugal), University of Rome TorVergata and Humanitas University in Milan (Italy). Coordinated by Dr Maria Carla Parrini. https://www.arturoproject.eu Therapy resistance remains a major challenge in oncology. Recent studies suggest that the intratumoral microbiome influences responses to anticancer treatments, particularly immunotherapy. The ARTURO project aims to better understand the role of bacteria and their metabolites in the tumor microenvironment and in drug response through an innovative 3D tumor-on-chip model integrating clinical data, multi-omics analyses, and state-of-the-art technologies. The research focuses on non-small cell lung cancer and invasive lobular breast cancer. Missions -        Perform bioinformatics analyses of transcriptomics data (bulk RNA-seq, deconvolution, scRNA-seq, and Visium HD spatial transcriptomics). -        Interact on a daily basis with experimental scientists generating the data. -        Conduct scientific and technological monitoring relevant to the project. -        Communicate analysis results through meetings, written reports, and scientific publications. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Master's degree or PhD in a field related to bioinformatics (the development of a PhD project on the topic is an available opportunity). -        Previous experience in the analysis of sequencing data (bulk RNA-seq, single-cell RNA-seq, and/or spatial transcriptomics). Skills required -        Fluent in English. -        Analysis of high-dimensional omics data. -        Proficiency in high-level programming languages such as Python and/or R, and familiarity with good coding practices. -        Strong interest in the analysis of complex and heterogeneous biological datasets. -        Desired personal qualities: autonomy, organizational skills, teamwork, and the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary environment. Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term contract Starting date: January 2026 Duration : 18 months Working time : full time Gross annual salary :  29240 € to 36219 €  according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 75%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references Publication date: 15/10/2026 Deadline for application: Once filled Faithful to the legacy of its founder, the Institut Curie is deeply committed to promoting equal opportunities, diversity, and inclusion. Convinced that diversity of backgrounds and experiences contributes to collective performance, we strive to provide everyone with a respectful and equitable working environment and encourage all candidates to apply for our job opportunities. All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+5, Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact 9jg1pw26y35k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 18 mois Quotité de travail Référence 9jg1pw26y3 Publié le 15/10/2026 Postuler Bioinformatician position in cancer research (F/M) (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  04/01/2027 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The Curie Institute Research Center France’s leading cancer research and treatment centre, Institut Curie unites a renowned research centre and a specialist hospital, fostering close collaboration between scientists, clinicians and healthcare professionals. It offers an environment of excellence where expertise comes together around shared values: care, humanity, openness, collaboration, efficiency, innovation, solidarity and commitment. Missions Activités principales Laboratory \"Chemical Biology of Cancer\" Unit - Director: Fatima Mechta-Grigoriou Institut Curie -  U1339 Inserm - UMR3666 CNRS “Stress and Cancer” Laboratory - Director: Fatima Mechta-Grigoriou https://curie.fr/equipe/mechta-grigoriou This position is associated with the ARTURO project, funded by the European Commission under the Horizon Europe programme (Cancer Mission 2023). International collaboration between Institut Curie and Assistance Publique Hôpitaux de Paris - Bichat hospital (France), Universidade Catolica Portugueasa and Fundação Gaspar Frutuoso (Portugal), University of Rome TorVergata and Humanitas University in Milan (Italy). Coordinated by Dr Maria Carla Parrini. https://www.arturoproject.eu Therapy resistance remains a major challenge in oncology. Recent studies suggest that the intratumoral microbiome influences responses to anticancer treatments, particularly immunotherapy. The ARTURO project aims to better understand the role of bacteria and their metabolites in the tumor microenvironment and in drug response through an innovative 3D tumor-on-chip model integrating clinical data, multi-omics analyses, and state-of-the-art technologies. The research focuses on non-small cell lung cancer and invasive lobular breast cancer. Missions -        Perform bioinformatics analyses of transcriptomics data (bulk RNA-seq, deconvolution, scRNA-seq, and Visium HD spatial transcriptomics). -        Interact on a daily basis with experimental scientists generating the data. -        Conduct scientific and technological monitoring relevant to the project. -        Communicate analysis results through meetings, written reports, and scientific publications. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Master's degree or PhD in a field related to bioinformatics (the development of a PhD project on the topic is an available opportunity). -        Previous experience in the analysis of sequencing data (bulk RNA-seq, single-cell RNA-seq, and/or spatial transcriptomics). Skills required -        Fluent in English. -        Analysis of high-dimensional omics data. -        Proficiency in high-level programming languages such as Python and/or R, and familiarity with good coding practices. -        Strong interest in the analysis of complex and heterogeneous biological datasets. -        Desired personal qualities: autonomy, organizational skills, teamwork, and the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary environment. Contract information Type of contract : Fixed-term contract Starting date: January 2026 Duration : 18 months Working time : full time Gross annual salary :  29240 € to 36219 €  according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 75%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Paris Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references Publication date: 15/10/2