    "https://recrutement.psl.eu/invr1ev15x": {
      "title": "Assistant Engineer (F/M)",
      "description": "Assistant Engineer (F/M) | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF Assistant Engineer (F/M) (F/H) Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The 'Chemistry and Modelling for Cancer Biology' unit (UMR9187) is located at the Institut Curie research centre in Orsay. It is an interdisciplinary unit dedicated to designing and synthesising molecular probes and anti-cancer drug candidates and studying their mechanisms of action. The unit comprises 50 people and is supported by: - three research teams. - Two cross-disciplinary divisions (modelling and biology). - the 'Chimiothèque' platform, which is one of the largest in France with almost 13,000 compounds resulting from 70 years of research. https://institut-curie.org/unit/umr9187-u1196 https://institut-curie.org/team/verga Missions Our team is looking for a motivated Assistant Engineer (AE) in biology to contribute to a project involving the development of therapeutic molecules. Description of the activities -        Ensure the culture of adherent cell lines (BS2) -        Perform cytotoxicity tests -        Perform IP1 (inositol monophosphate) dosage tests -        Perform proliferation and invasion tests -        Carry out RNA extraction and downstream analyses (RT-qPCR) -        Collaborate closely with researchers to analyze experimental data and contribute to the project's progress Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Education: Bac + 2 to Bac + 3 (BTS – Professional License - BUT) -        Experience: At least 1 to 2 years of practical experience in cell culture Knowledge -        Knowledge of cell and molecular biology -        Ability to analyze results obtained and write a laboratory notebook Desired operational skills -        Apply hygiene and safety rules -        Master basic cell culture techniques in L2 -        Maintain a high level of concentration during repetitive manipulations -        Demonstrate rigor in conducting experiments to ensure the quality and reliability of results -        Ensure the traceability of chemical compounds Skills required -        English proficiency: B1 to B2 -        IT skills: Microsoft Suite / Prism -        Good organizational skills, ability to work autonomously and in a team -        Rigor, motivation, and enthusiasm for research All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : CDD Starting date: 01/11/2026 Duration : 1 year Working time : full time - 39 hours per week Remuneration : from de 25131.77€ à 27504.77€ according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Orsay Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references, to Publication date: 02/10/2026 Deadline for application: 30/10/2026 Faithful to the legacy of its founder, the Institut Curie is deeply committed to promoting equal opportunities, diversity, and inclusion. Convinced that diversity of backgrounds and experiences contributes to collective performance, we strive to provide everyone with a respectful and equitable working environment and encourage all candidates to apply for our job opportunities. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+1/Bac+2 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact invr1ev15x5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération De 25131.77 à 27504.77 € (Euros) par an Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 1 an(s) Quotité de travail Référence invr1ev15x Publié le 22/10/2026 Postuler Assistant Engineer (F/M) (F/H) Localisation du poste 91400, Orsay, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil The “Institut Curie” is a major player in the research and fight against cancer. It consists of a hospital and a Research Center of more than 1000 employees with a strong international representativeness. The objective of the Curie Institute Research Center is to develop basic research and to use the knowledge produced to improve the diagnosis, prognosis, and therapeutics of cancers as part of the continuum between basic research and innovation serving the patient. Missions Activités principales Laboratory The 'Chemistry and Modelling for Cancer Biology' unit (UMR9187) is located at the Institut Curie research centre in Orsay. It is an interdisciplinary unit dedicated to designing and synthesising molecular probes and anti-cancer drug candidates and studying their mechanisms of action. The unit comprises 50 people and is supported by: - three research teams. - Two cross-disciplinary divisions (modelling and biology). - the 'Chimiothèque' platform, which is one of the largest in France with almost 13,000 compounds resulting from 70 years of research. https://institut-curie.org/unit/umr9187-u1196 https://institut-curie.org/team/verga Missions Our team is looking for a motivated Assistant Engineer (AE) in biology to contribute to a project involving the development of therapeutic molecules. Description of the activities -        Ensure the culture of adherent cell lines (BS2) -        Perform cytotoxicity tests -        Perform IP1 (inositol monophosphate) dosage tests -        Perform proliferation and invasion tests -        Carry out RNA extraction and downstream analyses (RT-qPCR) -        Collaborate closely with researchers to analyze experimental data and contribute to the project's progress Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Training and experience required -        Education: Bac + 2 to Bac + 3 (BTS – Professional License - BUT) -        Experience: At least 1 to 2 years of practical experience in cell culture Knowledge -        Knowledge of cell and molecular biology -        Ability to analyze results obtained and write a laboratory notebook Desired operational skills -        Apply hygiene and safety rules -        Master basic cell culture techniques in L2 -        Maintain a high level of concentration during repetitive manipulations -        Demonstrate rigor in conducting experiments to ensure the quality and reliability of results -        Ensure the traceability of chemical compounds Skills required -        English proficiency: B1 to B2 -        IT skills: Microsoft Suite / Prism -        Good organizational skills, ability to work autonomously and in a team -        Rigor, motivation, and enthusiasm for research All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities Contract information Type of contract : CDD Starting date: 01/11/2026 Duration : 1 year Working time : full time - 39 hours per week Remuneration : from de 25131.77€ à 27504.77€ according to the current grids Benefits: Collective catering, reimbursement of transportation fees up to 70%, supplementary health insurance Location of the position : Orsay Contact Please send your CV, letter of motivation and 2 references, to Publication date: 02/10/2026 Deadline for application: 30/10/2026 Faithful to the legacy of its founder, the Institut Curie is deeply committed to promoting equal opportunities, diversity, and inclusion. Convinced that diversity of backgrounds and experiences contributes to collective performance, we strive to provide everyone with a respectful and equitable working environment and encourage all candidates to apply for our job opportunities. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+3, Bac+1/Bac+2 Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact invr1ev15x5k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération : De 25131.77 à 27504.77 € (Euros) par an Type de contrat / de poste : CDD Durée du contrat : 1 an(s) Référence invr1ev15x Publié le 22/10/2026 L'Université PSL (Paris Sciences & Lettres) Menu Footer RH CGU Crédits Politique de confidentialité Flux RSS de PSL Recrutement Gestion des cookies Vos paramètres de cookies Vous naviguez sur le site de l’Université PSL. L’Université PSL, responsable de traitement, utilise des cookies pour la réalisation de statistiques ainsi que pour l’optimisation du site. Vous pouvez accepter ou refuser l’utilisation de cookies, ainsi que personnaliser vos préférences. Nous conservons votre choix pendant 3 mois. Vous pouvez changer d’avis à tout moment en cliquant sur l’icône « Gestion des cookies » en bas à gauche sur toutes les pages de notre site internet. Plus d'informations Cookies obligatoire (session Drupal) Ces cookies sont strictement obligatoires au bon fonctionnent du site. Cookies vidéos Ils permettent la visualisation des vidéos sur notre site. (Youtube) Cookies de mesure d'audience Enregistrer mes choix Tout accepter Personnaliser"
